00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:56,820
know how to visualize spots using TLC stains as well as UV light. This video

6
00:00:56,820 --> 00:01:00,820
will cover the advanced techniques involved in carrying out thin layer

7
00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:07,460
chromatography. In the basic TLC video, you learned how to set up a developing

8
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:14,500
chamber, mark and spot a TLC plate, develop the plate, visualize the spots

9
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:22,620
using a UV lamp, and calculate RF values. You also learned how to choose a

10
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:27,740
developing solvent and compare the identity of two compounds using a co-spot.

11
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:34,020
This video will demonstrate some advanced techniques commonly used in

12
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:39,740
research laboratories. You will learn how to cut glass TLC plates from large

13
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:45,580
plates, how to pull spotters from capillary tubes, and how to stain TLC

14
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:54,830
plates to visualize spots. Let's start out with the TLC plates. Plastic backed

15
00:01:54,830 --> 00:01:59,670
TLC plates, such as those used in the basic video, are found in many

16
00:01:59,670 --> 00:02:05,990
laboratories because they are cheap, usually pre-cut into a usable size, and

17
00:02:05,990 --> 00:02:13,590
if not, easy to cut with scissors. In spite of these conveniences, many

18
00:02:13,590 --> 00:02:20,070
chemists prefer glass backed TLC plates. They can withstand more heat than a

19
00:02:20,070 --> 00:02:24,030
plastic backed plate, which is important when you are using stains to

20
00:02:24,030 --> 00:02:31,860
visualize spots. They also frequently offer better resolution. Unlike plastic

21
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:36,940
plates, glass plates are generally purchased as large squares, approximately

22
00:02:36,940 --> 00:02:43,340
20 centimeters by 20 centimeters. This means that it's up to you to cut the

23
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:49,780
plate into smaller plates of usable size. With a few well-placed cuts, you

24
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:56,300
can generally get approximately 40 to 60 small plates from one big plate. The

25
00:02:56,300 --> 00:03:02,740
small plates are commonly 5 centimeters long and about 1 to 2 centimeters wide.

26
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:08,180
Cutting glass TLC plates without breaking them is something of an art. It will

27
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:14,570
take some practice, but here are a few tips to get you started. First, you will

28
00:03:14,570 --> 00:03:19,010
need a glass cutter, like the one shown here, to score the glass and allow

29
00:03:19,010 --> 00:03:24,970
you to break it in a straight line. Start by making three well-placed cuts,

30
00:03:25,010 --> 00:03:31,210
approximately 5 centimeters apart. This will give you four long strips that can

31
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:38,920
be cut into individual plates. Start by placing the large glass plate, adsorbent

32
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:44,800
side down, on a clean dry surface. Use a pencil and a ruler to mark the cuts

33
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:51,050
that you are going to make. Next, use the glass cutter to score a line in the

34
00:03:51,050 --> 00:03:56,930
plate. You may be tempted to score the plate repeatedly to deepen the cut in

35
00:03:56,930 --> 00:04:02,450
the glass, but this will actually make it more difficult to break the plate in

36
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:10,260
a clean straight line. Instead, firmly score the glass with one sweep of the

37
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:19,580
glass cutter, and using the edge of your bench for support, break the plate

38
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:25,700
in a clean straight line. Continue cutting the long strip into individual

39
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:31,980
TLC plates until you have amassed a nice stockpile. With your plates ready to

40
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:38,830
go, now it's time to pull some TLC spotters. While commercially available

41
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:43,990
capillary spotters can be used to apply samples to TLC plates, many people

42
00:04:43,990 --> 00:04:48,950
prefer to pull their own spotters. This is because pulled spotters have a

43
00:04:48,950 --> 00:04:53,950
smaller diameter, so you can apply smaller spots to the plate. This means

44
00:04:53,950 --> 00:04:58,310
that you get better resolution, and you're able to spot more spots per

45
00:04:58,310 --> 00:05:04,070
plate. Because you can conserve plates, this makes pulling your own spotters the

46
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:11,340
economical choice. Put the center of a capillary tube into the blue flame from

47
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:18,020
a Bunsen burner, and hold it there until the center starts to soften. Then, remove

48
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:23,620
the capillary from the flame and pull on the ends of the tube. This causes

49
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:29,300
the center of the tube to stretch and narrow. This will take a little bit of

50
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:33,500
practice. If the tube isn't hot enough when you pull it, you won't be able to

51
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:37,460
stretch it, but if you leave it in the flame for too long, it'll turn into a

52
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:43,950
saggy mess. Once you have heated and pulled the capillary tube, break it into

53
00:05:43,950 --> 00:05:51,000
two pieces at the center. You should end up with two fine tipped TLC spotters

54
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:57,640
from every capillary tube. With a bit more experience and in a settling torch,

55
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:03,960
you can also pull TLC spotters from pasture or pipettes. On a good day, you can

56
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:09,440
get dozens of TLC spotters from one pipette, but for safety reasons, this

57
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:15,620
technique is best learned from an experienced lab mate. With your plates

58
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:21,620
and spotters in hand, you're ready to learn about using some TLC stains. A

59
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:27,580
standard TLC station in an organic laboratory consists of a UV lamp, which

60
00:06:27,580 --> 00:06:34,220
you learned about in the basic video, a variety of TLC stains, some paper towels,

61
00:06:34,220 --> 00:06:42,800
and a heat source, either a heat gun or a hot plate. Before you do any staining,

62
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:48,480
spot and develop your plate as usual and allow all of the solvent to evaporate

63
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:59,430
from the surface. Then, dip your plate into the stain. Allow excess stain to

64
00:06:59,430 --> 00:07:09,220
drain back into the jar and dry the back of the plate on a paper towel. Don't be

65
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:13,660
discouraged if you don't see any spots on your plate just yet. You have to heat

66
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:19,820
the plate to activate the stain. Turn on the heat gun and hold the plate just

67
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:27,780
above the barrel. Watch closely and you should see your spots appear. Don't heat

68
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:35,970
for too long or you'll end up with a blackened TLC plate. While numerous TLC

69
00:07:35,970 --> 00:07:42,370
stains have been developed, some good common ones are phosphomalibtic acid, PMA,

70
00:07:42,370 --> 00:07:51,080
cirrhic ammonium molybdenate, CAM, and potassium permanganate. Let's finish up

71
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:57,240
with a few general tips for using TLC stains. Remember that staining is a

72
00:07:57,240 --> 00:08:02,520
destructive form of visualization. The stain will react irreversibly with the

73
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:07,600
compounds on your plate. This means that you should always view your plate under

74
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:14,520
the UV lamp prior to staining. Not all compounds will show up in all stains, so

75
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:18,880
you may have to screen a variety of stains to find one that works for you.

76
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:25,830
Remember, this video is intended to help you prepare for lab by providing a

77
00:08:25,830 --> 00:08:30,470
demonstration of the proper experimental technique. It is not intended

78
00:08:30,470 --> 00:08:34,910
as a replacement for reading your lab manual or the supplementary material. In

79
00:08:34,910 --> 00:08:39,470
order to become a great experimentalist, it is important that you understand both

80
00:08:39,470 --> 00:08:45,310
theory and technique. Now it's your turn. Good luck!
